A||N||4||DaRkLoRD||Questions about a 2.8 head gasket: cost, installation, etc||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||01-15-2001||02:03 PM||||As part of a tune-up, I want to get all the sensors replaced, as well as the belts, head gasket, plugs & wires, etc..<P>I'm sure belts are cheap, and I already have a good idea of how much sensors cost.. but how much is a new head gasket? I was told they're expensive..?<BR>Also, how hard is it to replace this stuff myself? I know a bit about engines, but I have practically no hands-on experience. I'm a quick learner though.. I'm quite good at mechanical stuff..<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||01-15-2001||02:20 PM||||To me at least for a tune up head gaskets seem like overkill.  I would have to say leave well enough alone.  Now if you are having problems that is a different story.   <P>I have changed other head gaskets but not on a Fiero.  They are rather simple, at least in the RWD applicaions I have done.  Only special tool you need is a torque wrench.  Also you need to check that the block and head surfaces are flat, this should not be a problem since there is no problem now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||01-15-2001||04:23 PM||||I did that about 2 months back. Not very hard, but not somthing I am anxious to do again either. Its really not hard, just time consuming. I agree head gaskets as a tuneup item are overkill, but if the car has never had them replaced, and you are willing to part with it, go ahead and do it so you can ensure you wont have any trouble with it in the future. Just make sure to lable a lot!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||01-15-2001||06:29 PM||||Here's some idea of the material costs involved in removing the heads on a V6 engine...<P>As I recall, Fel-Pro head gaskets cost about $15 each.  You will also need the intake gasket set (plenum, intake manifold, throttle body, etc.)  Although the Fel-Pro set includes some kind of valve cover gaskets, they DO NOT fit the Fiero V6.  Add another $20 or so for these.  Then you will need a new set of head bolts, which cost about $26 at Auto Zone and Fiero Store, $35 at Pep Boys.  These bolts are designed to stretch when they are torqued...DO NOT reuse the old head bolts. <P>After you pull the heads, you should chase the head bolt threads in the block with a 11mm x 1.5 tap, about $6 at NAPA.  This will remove the remnants of the sealer used on the head bolts and will ensure proper head bolt tensioning.  While the heads are off, you may as well replace the valve stem seals....about $20.  Gee, while you're at it, port/fix the exhaust manifolds and replace the exhaust manifold gaskets (about $26 for the gaskets alone).  If you go this far, it may be cheaper to buy a "head gasket set" which should include the head gaskets, intake, plenum, exhaust manifold and valve cover gaskets (basically everything down to the block).  Add another $20 or so for paint, thread sealer, etc. and you begin to see that this is rapidly becomming a fairly expensive job.<P>Pulling the heads is not for the faint of heart, but it is doable. In my opinion, I wouldn't do it again unless I had a pretty good reason!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>     <p>[This message has been edited by Mark (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||01-15-2001||08:11 PM||||AAAAAHHH!<P>ok, nevermind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||11
